      {
        "id": 202065,
        "name": "Phantom5613",
        "username": "Phantom5613",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/{size}/1906_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-08-23T14:49:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>PDFs are all well and good, but just don't get to the level of dependency on electronics MY group is at.</p><p>It's gotten to the point that no one but me uses paper sheets anymore, and there's hardly any room to roll actual dice because everyone has to have their computers out to see their character sheets...</p><p>\" 'Book'? What kind of a download file&nbsp;is that?\"</p><p>And don't get me started on how if it isn't their turn then they start up a videogame or are web brousing, and therefore have no idea what's going on when it IS their turn...</p><p>Again, I don't outright hate PDFs. I just hate how my group has forgotten that paper is a thing...</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:30:42.538Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
