        "id": 202071,
        "name": "Phantom5613",
        "username": "Phantom5613",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/{size}/1906_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-08-24T04:20:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Silverleaf\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/48/2332_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Silverleaf:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I prefer to save trees and fuel for transportation and cash for shipping and keep that stuff electronic.Sometimes I don't even refer to the PDF at all during sessions but it's nice to have it there.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I'm almost positive that running at least 3-4 plugged-in laptops constantly for multiple sessions each week eats up more energy/resourses compared to printing/transporting one 200+ page book.</p>\n<p>Also, just looked this up, America has had tree farms since 1941 apparently, and has been used to harvest needed fibers and paper for the country.</p>",
